cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "M³-AVM: Research Prototype for Sparse Event-Driven Tensor Computation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Marques"
    given-names: "Matheus de Camargo"
    email: "matheuscamarques@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/matheuscamarques/m3_avm"
url: "https://github.com/matheuscamarques/m3_avm"
abstract: "M³-AVM (Máquina Abstrata de Matheus de Camargo Marques) is a deterministic virtual machine prototype in Rust for sparse event-driven tensor computation: fixed 15-opcode ISA (32-byte instructions), strict-priority scheduler with preemption (FORK/ABORT), CSR sparse tensors, GGUF mmap inference with KV-cache rollback, and optional wgpu acceleration."
keywords:
  - virtual-machine
  - tensor
  - sparse-computation
  - rust
  - ai-infrastructure
  - preemption
  - kv-cache
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-09"
